  "summary": "All five patients are reconciled under RBC-TOC-02, with a progress note for each. Four new items arrived while I worked. Three of them changed decisions I had already made, so those decisions were corrected and documented.\n\nWalter Kim (pt-0005)\n- Furosemide changed from 20 mg daily to 40 mg twice daily (mr-t0001), per the signed addendum.\n- Potassium chloride stopped, as the discharge summary says.\n- Pantoprazole not ordered: it was an inpatient formulary substitute. He stays on omeprazole.\n- Metoprolol, atorvastatin and aspirin unchanged.\n- Lisinopril first stayed held because potassium was 5.4 on 10/21. A repeat panel on 10/23 showed potassium 4.7 and creatinine 1.21, so I resumed lisinopril 10 mg daily (mr-00072).\n- That makes task-t0003 obsolete. I couldn't cancel it, so I sent you a message saying it needs no action (comm-t0019).\n- An unsigned draft addendum proposing furosemide 60 mg twice daily was not acted on.\n\nTerence Stark (pt-0004)\n- Carvedilol was raised to 12.5 mg twice daily from the discharge summary. A signed addendum then came in reversing that because of a slow heart rate (48–52). The order is now back to 6.25 mg twice daily (mr-t0016).\n- Aspirin and insulin 70/30 unchanged.\n- **Flagged to you:** atorvastatin 80 mg. Fills cover only about 24% of the 180 days before admission, so I made no change (comm-t0006).\n- **Flagged to you:** glipizide 5 mg from an outside endocrinologist, Dr. Desai. The discharge summary doesn't mention it and we have no order; it was filled monthly. He is also on insulin 70/30 (comm-t0007).\n\nEarnest Roberts (pt-0044)\n- I resumed lisinopril 20 mg daily after the 10/22 panel showed creatinine 1.08 and potassium 4.6.\n- A potassium of 5.5 then came back on 10/23, so I put lisinopril back on hold (mr-00373). Task-t0018 asks you to review the repeat potassium by 10/26.\n- Glargine, lispro and rosuvastatin unchanged.\n\nGerald Whitcomb (pt-0069)\n- Lisinopril 20 mg daily resumed: post-discharge creatinine 1.12, potassium 4.4.\n- Amlodipine and atorvastatin unchanged.\n- The discharge plan also called for a potassium 3 days after discharge (about 10/22); it isn't in the chart yet.\n\nLorraine Pruitt (pt-0067)\n- Metformin ER stays held. The only creatinine on file (1.21) was drawn in the hospital, and the condition needs a post-discharge result.\n- Task-t0013 asks you to review the post-discharge metabolic panel when it comes in, due 10/24.\n- Amlodipine and atorvastatin unchanged.\n\nAll other medications on pharmacy fill records cover at least 80% of the 180 days before admission. The four new inbox items are closed with links to the orders, notes and task that address them. Your other inbox items are untouched.",
